From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: guest writes change page protection after the buffer cache lock (zortos293/Lichii #1518 2dad3db, lucastaonline's f5902c6c68 from #1161), off by default

Switch: EDEN_UP_DEFER_PROTECT=1 (exact "1", read once, at the first guest write). Off, or any other
value: exactly T146. On, the first guest write logs "EDEN_UP_DEFER_PROTECT: guest writes change page
protection after the buffer cache lock" (LOG_INFO).

What: RasterizerVulkan::OnCPUWrite holds buffer_cache.mutex while the pages a guest write untracks
change their host protection (UpdatePagesCachedBatch -> MarkRegionCaching, a system call per run).
Every other thread that wants the lock, the GPU back thread before its draws among them, waits for
those calls; upstream counts thousands a second at the water. With the switch on, a guest thread
that does not own the Vulkan scheduler collects its page untracking (-1) while it holds the lock
and applies it, in the order made, right after it drops the lock. The word state still changes
under the lock as before. Tracking (+1) is never deferred: applied at once, so a page is never
tracked later than its words say. Off the owner a write only untracks pages
(BufferCache::WriteMemory uploads only on the owner, keep_page_gpu_data && OwnsScheduler()).

Unmap: the first deferred batch raises DeviceMemoryManager's in-flight count while the lock is still
held, the apply lowers it; Unmap waits for 0 after InvalidateRegion (which takes the buffer cache
lock, so it orders after any write that deferred under it). A -1 applied after the page lost its
backing would be dropped, the page would keep its count and a remap's upload would never protect
the new backing.

Why a switch and not unconditional: it is not a pure bug fix. It moves system calls out of a lock
and adds a wait to Unmap: a speed change with new interleavings (a page stays protected a little
longer after its words are untracked: a write that traps there finds nothing to do, upstream's
argument; a writer that retries on our guest memory service may trap more than once in that
window). Unmeasured by upstream (no fps number in the PR). Off cost: one cached bool test per guest
write in OnCPUWrite, one thread-local pointer test per ApplyCollectedRanges (the pointer is only
set with the switch on), one load of a counter that is always 0 in Unmap.

Frame-ahead guard: the guard arms and lifts its pages with its own UpdatePagesCachedBatch(+1/-1)
calls on the device memory (ahead_guard.h), not through WordManager, so none of its calls is
deferred. Page counts add up in any order; a deferred -1 only holds a count higher than the words
for a moment, never lower, so a page the guard armed stays protected exactly as before. No guard
patch (0491, 0492, 0504, 0630, 0631) touches ApplyCollectedRanges or OnCPUWrite; 0229 made the
batch path this branch sits in. The code sits beside 0317 (EDEN_PE_CPU_WRITE_AHEAD) and 0421
(EDEN_UP_HELD_VS_DOWNLOAD) in OnCPUWrite: both run inside the deferral scope (their untracking is
deferred too), the held path's texture cache write runs after the apply. prepare-vulkan-port.py's
two anchors in OnCPUWrite (the timer after the signature, the GuestCacheLock spin on the buffer
cache lock) still match: the scope object is made on the line before the lock, so it ends after the
lock is dropped on every way out, the early return included.

Not taken from upstream: its unit tests (our core has no src/tests), its ASSERT on a +1 (here a +1
is just applied at once, as its release path does), its Nx2Perf::Verify branch (not in ours).
Not in the shader-prep TranslationSwitches: it changes no translation, so both arms keep one store.

Origin and credit: lucastaonline, commit f5902c6c68 in zortos293/Lichii PR #1161; ported to Lichii
nx2 by zortos293 as 2dad3db (PR #1518, merged 12 Nov), whose Unmap wait and owner-only rule are
taken here.
---
diff --git a/src/core/device_memory_manager.h b/src/core/device_memory_manager.h
index 95ebfb5..0440573 100644
--- a/src/core/device_memory_manager.h
+++ b/src/core/device_memory_manager.h
@@ -137,6 +137,18 @@ public:
     // New batch API to update multiple ranges with a single lock acquisition.
     void UpdatePagesCachedBatch(std::span<const std::pair<DAddr, size_t>> ranges, s32 delta);
 
+    /// EDEN_UP_DEFER_PROTECT (0655, Lichii #1518 2dad3db): held by a thread from before it drops
+    /// the buffer cache lock it untracked pages under until it has applied their count changes
+    /// (RasterizerVulkan::OnCPUWrite). Unmap waits for every holder after invalidating the range:
+    /// a change applied once the page has no backing is lost, and the page would keep its count
+    /// and never be protected again. Never taken with the switch off.
+    void BeginDeferredCachedUpdates() {
+        deferred_cached_updates.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    }
+    void EndDeferredCachedUpdates() {
+        deferred_cached_updates.fetch_sub(1, std::memory_order_release);
+    }
+
     /// Traps the next guest CPU read of these pages, to learn which GPU writes the CPU reads.
     void ArmReadTraps(DAddr addr, size_t size);
 
@@ -274,6 +286,7 @@ private:
     std::unique_ptr<CachedPages> cached_pages;
     Common::RangeMutex counter_guard;
     std::mutex mapping_guard;
+    std::atomic<u32> deferred_cached_updates{}; ///< 0655: always 0 with EDEN_UP_DEFER_PROTECT off
 
 
 };
diff --git a/src/core/device_memory_manager.inc b/src/core/device_memory_manager.inc
index 265f11e..a370858 100644
--- a/src/core/device_memory_manager.inc
+++ b/src/core/device_memory_manager.inc
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <atomic>
 #include <limits>
 #include <memory>
+#include <thread>
 #include <type_traits>
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <vector>
@@ -303,6 +304,12 @@ void DeviceMemoryManager<Traits>::Unmap(DAddr address, size_t size) {
     size_t start_page_d = address >> Memory::YUZU_PAGEBITS;
     size_t num_pages = Common::AlignUp(size, Memory::YUZU_PAGESIZE) >> Memory::YUZU_PAGEBITS;
     device_inter->InvalidateRegion(address, size);
+    // 0655 (EDEN_UP_DEFER_PROTECT): page count changes a guest write took out of the buffer
+    // cache's lock land before the backing goes. With the switch off the count is never raised:
+    // one load of 0.
+    while (deferred_cached_updates.load(std::memory_order_acquire) != 0) {
+        std::this_thread::yield();
+    }
     std::scoped_lock lk(mapping_guard);
 
     tracked_entries.CommitRegion(start_page_d, start_page_d + num_pages); // should already be committed, but just in case
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/word_manager.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/word_manager.h
index 0a132ed..b3d448a 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/word_manager.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/word_manager.h
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <memory>
 #include <limits>
 #include <span>
+#include <cstddef>
 #include <utility>
 #include <vector>
 
@@ -39,6 +40,68 @@ enum class Type {
     Max
 };
 
+/// EDEN_UP_DEFER_PROTECT=1 (0655; Lichii #1518 2dad3db, lucastaonline's f5902c6c68 from #1161):
+/// page untracking a guest thread applies itself once it drops the buffer cache's lock
+/// (RasterizerVulkan::OnCPUWrite). Changing a page's host protection is a system call, and every
+/// other thread drawing or reading waited for it. Only untracking waits: a page protected a little
+/// longer traps a write that then finds it untracked, but a page tracked late lets a write through
+/// unseen. The first deferred batch raises the tracker's in-flight count (under the lock), the
+/// apply lowers it again; DeviceMemoryManager::Unmap waits for it.
+class DeferredPageCaching {
+public:
+    using Ranges = std::vector<std::pair<VAddr, size_t>>;
+    using Apply = void (*)(void* tracker, std::span<const std::pair<VAddr, size_t>>, s32 delta);
+    using End = void (*)(void* tracker);
+
+    void Add(void* tracker, Apply apply, End end, const Ranges& ranges, s32 delta) {
+        if (batches.empty()) {
+            end_tracker = tracker;
+            end_call = end;
+        }
+        batches.push_back(Batch{tracker, apply, delta, collected.size(), ranges.size()});
+        collected.insert(collected.end(), ranges.begin(), ranges.end());
+    }
+
+    /// In the order they were made: one page can be untracked and tracked again in between.
+    void ApplyAll() {
+        for (const Batch& batch : batches) {
+            batch.apply(batch.tracker,
+                        std::span<const std::pair<VAddr, size_t>>(collected).subspan(batch.begin,
+                                                                                    batch.count),
+                        batch.delta);
+        }
+        const bool had = !batches.empty();
+        batches.clear();
+        collected.clear();
+        if (had && end_call != nullptr) {
+            end_call(end_tracker);
+        }
+        end_tracker = nullptr;
+        end_call = nullptr;
+    }
+
+    [[nodiscard]] bool Empty() const {
+        return batches.empty();
+    }
+
+private:
+    struct Batch {
+        void* tracker;
+        Apply apply;
+        s32 delta;
+        size_t begin;
+        size_t count;
+    };
+    std::vector<Batch> batches;
+    Ranges collected;
+    void* end_tracker{};
+    End end_call{};
+};
+
+/// Set while the calling thread collects its page untracking instead of applying it (0655; only
+/// RasterizerVulkan::OnCPUWrite sets it, and only with EDEN_UP_DEFER_PROTECT=1).
+inline thread_local DeferredPageCaching* t_deferred_page_caching{};
+
 // EDEN_UP_HOT_PAGES=1 (exact "1", off without it; Frizti/Fritchii d20c32704c, there
 // EDEN_NX2_EXP48, a port of Eglantine f27522bfb9 by kraibse): a page the CPU rewrites again and
 // again is no longer write-trapped after each upload. It uploads once a frame instead, whether it
@@ -424,6 +487,27 @@ struct WordManager {
             }
         }
         coalesced.emplace_back(cur_addr, cur_size);
+        // 0655 (EDEN_UP_DEFER_PROTECT): untracking waits until the write drops the lock. Tracking
+        // (+1) is applied at once, so a page is never tracked later than its words say.
+        if (DeferredPageCaching* const deferred = t_deferred_page_caching;
+            deferred != nullptr && delta < 0) {
+            if (deferred->Empty()) {
+                tracker->BeginDeferredCachedUpdates();
+            }
+            deferred->Add(
+                tracker,
+                [](void* deferred_tracker, std::span<const std::pair<VAddr, size_t>> runs,
+                   s32 run_delta) {
+                    static_cast<DeviceTracker*>(deferred_tracker)
+                        ->UpdatePagesCachedBatch(runs, run_delta);
+                },
+                [](void* deferred_tracker) {
+                    static_cast<DeviceTracker*>(deferred_tracker)->EndDeferredCachedUpdates();
+                },
+                coalesced, delta);
+            ranges.clear();
+            return;
+        }
         // Use batch API to reduce lock acquisitions and contention.
         tracker->UpdatePagesCachedBatch(coalesced, delta);
         ranges.clear();
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
index 85b401e..fb0a426 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
@@ -2684,8 +2684,44 @@ bool RasterizerVulkan::OnCPUWrite(DAddr addr, u64 size) {
     // texture cache, so the images over it don't download their older bytes over it before it
     // is applied. Only the pipeline cache waits for the apply.
     static const bool held_vs_download = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_HELD_VS_DOWNLOAD");
+    // EDEN_UP_DEFER_PROTECT=1 (0655; Lichii #1518 2dad3db, lucastaonline's f5902c6c68 from #1161):
+    // the pages this write untracks change their host protection after the buffer cache's lock is
+    // dropped, not under it: drawing waited for those system calls (~1 us each, thousands a second
+    // at the water). A write trapping on a page still protected until then finds it already
+    // untracked and changes nothing. Off the scheduler's owner a write only untracks pages
+    // (BufferCache::WriteMemory uploads only on the owner), which is all that waits. Device
+    // unmaps wait for these changes (DeviceMemoryManager::BeginDeferredCachedUpdates). The scope
+    // is made before the lock, so it ends after the lock is dropped, on every way out.
+    static const bool defer_protect = [] {
+        const bool on = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_DEFER_PROTECT");
+        if (on) {
+            LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan, "EDEN_UP_DEFER_PROTECT: guest writes change page protection "
+                                    "after the buffer cache lock");
+        }
+        return on;
+    }();
+    struct DeferProtectScope {
+        VideoCommon::DeferredPageCaching* deferred{};
+        explicit DeferProtectScope(bool on) {
+            if (on && VideoCommon::t_deferred_page_caching == nullptr &&
+                !VideoCommon::GpuSplit::OwnsScheduler()) {
+                static thread_local VideoCommon::DeferredPageCaching thread_deferred;
+                deferred = &thread_deferred;
+                VideoCommon::t_deferred_page_caching = deferred;
+            }
+        }
+        ~DeferProtectScope() {
+            if (deferred != nullptr) {
+                VideoCommon::t_deferred_page_caching = nullptr;
+                deferred->ApplyAll();
+            }
+        }
+        DeferProtectScope(const DeferProtectScope&) = delete;
+        DeferProtectScope& operator=(const DeferProtectScope&) = delete;
+    };
     bool held = false;
     {
+        DeferProtectScope defer_scope{defer_protect};
         std::scoped_lock lock{buffer_cache.mutex};
         if (buffer_cache.OnCPUWrite(addr, size)) {
             if (!held_vs_download) {
